{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SeMrhayVnUsXi9e1Gc5txw","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md b/reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md\nindex 7ec6b0c..ee4cc30 100644\n--- a/reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md\n+++ b/reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md\n@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@\n-# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D16, 2026-10-16)\n+# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D17, 2026-10-17)\n \n What the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\n id `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ id `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verifi\n registered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\n when one exists but is not built yet).\n **Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\n-In-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:82`: stdlib subset +\n+In-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:112`: stdlib subset +\n `pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regipy / olefile /\n oletools / dnfile / LnkParse3 / lief / cryptography / asn1crypto / dpkt / PIL / `sqlite3` / `mailbox` / `wave` are\n worker-only (LLM side) until the allowlist is widened. See gaps `gate-allowlist-*`.\n@@ -20,6 +20,16 @@ plus deeper fields of already-seen families (timed kits are cumulative, D15 adde\n messages ... stable message identities\"). PE stayed three days (D9-11) with a deeper field each day, so D17-D19 most\n plausibly ask deeper `email.*` fields (In-Reply-To / References / attachments / Received / auth) or a sibling mail\n container (MBOX, Outlook MSG), then cross-message threading as a synthesis question. GM fmt word is `email`, not `eml`.\n+**D17 jumped to audio instead** (`media.primary_audio_codec_name` of one PCM `.wav` -> `pcm_s16le`; id\n+`d17-audio-001-media-...`: family `audio`, fmt `media`, ffprobe vocabulary). Flavor: \"Voice notes have been\n+transcoded, renamed, and embedded in mail. Determine the actual codecs, connect equivalent recordings, and find the\n+stream that breaks the sender's story.\" -> D18-D20 most plausibly: the same `media.*` namespace on OTHER containers/\n+codecs (renamed `.wav` that is MP3/Ogg-Opus/M4A/AMR -- \"actual codecs\"), deeper ffprobe stream fields (sample_rate,\n+channels, duration, bit_rate, format_name, stream count), a multi-stream container where one stream disagrees\n+(\"stream that breaks the story\": language/creation_time/encoder/codec), audio as a MIME attachment inside `.eml`\n+(\"embedded in mail\" -- D16 + D17 combined), and a cross-recording equivalence synthesis (\"connect equivalent\n+recordings\": same INFO title / correlation id / PCM payload / duration). Video `media.*` (h264 etc.) is the next step\n+after that. Email fields remain warm (D16 family carries over in every timed kit).\n \n ## 1. Atlas\n \n@@ -90,7 +100,7 @@ container (MBOX, Outlook MSG), then cross-message threading as a synthesis quest\n | 63 | PNG ancillary: tEXt/iTXt/zTXt, tIME, chunk order, bit depth/colour type, data after IEND | gap (target png-text-time) | chunk walk after sig | struct + zlib; `pngcheck -t -v` (I) | med-high -- D5 family |\n | 64 | GIF version / logical screen / frame count / comment ext; BMP DIB dims; ICO count | prebuilt gif/bmp/ico/wav | `GIF89a` w,h u16LE @6; `BM`; `00 00 01 00` | struct; `identify` (I) | med |\n | 65 | MP4/MOV: ftyp major brand, mvhd creation_time (1904 epoch), duration, `©xyz` GPS, `©too` encoder | gap | `ftyp` @4 | box walk struct; `mediainfo --Output=JSON` (I); `pymediainfo`/`ffprobe` (M) | low-med |\n-| 66 | Audio tags: ID3v2 TIT2/TPE1/COMM/APIC, ID3v1; WAV fmt + LIST/INFO; FLAC STREAMINFO + VORBIS_COMMENT | prebuilt mp3/wav (FLAC gap) | `ID3` @0 / `TAG` @-128; `RIFF..WAVE`; `fLaC` | `mutagen.File(io.BytesIO(b))` (M); `wave` stdlib; `exiftool -j` (I) | low-med |\n+| 66 | Audio tags: ID3v2 TIT2/TPE1/COMM/APIC, ID3v1; WAV fmt + LIST/INFO; FLAC STREAMINFO + VORBIS_COMMENT | prebuilt mp3/wav as fmt `mp3`/`wav` only -- NOT under GM fmt `media` (FLAC gap) | `ID3` @0 / `TAG` @-128; `RIFF..WAVE`; `fLaC` | `mutagen.File(io.BytesIO(b))` (I .venv, worker-only); `exifto\n | 67 | GZIP header: FNAME, MTIME, OS, ISIZE; BZ2/XZ magic | prebuilt gzip | `1f 8b 08`, flags @3, mtime u32LE @4, OS @9 | struct; `gzip -lv` | med |\n | 68 | TAR: member names, ustar magic, mtime, uname/gname, mode | gap | `ustar` @257 | `tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b))` | med |\n | 69 | 7z signature header version / RAR4 vs RAR5 / encrypted headers | gap | `37 7a bc af 27 1c` ver @6; `Rar!\\x1a\\x07\\x00` / `\\x01\\x00` | `7z l -slt` (I); `py7zr`/`rarfile` (M) | med (D7 title punned 7z) |\n@@ -117,6 +127,12 @@ container (MBOX, Outlook MSG), then cross-message threading as a synthesis quest\n | 90 | iCalendar / vCard: UID, ORGANIZER, ATTENDEE, DTSTART, SUMMARY; FN, EMAIL, TEL, ORG | gap (ics-vcard) | `BEGIN:VCALENDAR` / `BEGIN:VCARD` | RFC 5545/6350 line unfolding + `KEY;PARAM=..:value` split | low-med (mail attachment) |\n | 91 | `.library-ms` / `.searchConnector-ms` / `.url` phishing shortcuts | gap (url-library-ms) | XML `libraryDescription` ns / `[InternetShortcut]` | `xml.etree` local-name; configparser | low-med |\n | 92 | TNEF `winmail.dat`: attachment names, message class | gap (tnef-winmail) | `78 9f 3e 22` @0 | struct attribute walk | low |\n+| 93 | `media.primary_audio_codec_name` (ffprobe `codec_name` of stream a:0) | seen D17 (`pcm_s16le`; day17 solver `_audio_codec`, not yet in lib) | `RIFF..WAVE` `fmt ` tag+bits; other containers by magic | day17 `solve.py:_audio_codec`; `ffprobe -show_entries stream=codec_name` (M) | high -- every\n+| 94 | `media.*` stream/format fields: sample_rate, channels, channel_layout, bits_per_sample, sample_fmt, bit_rate, duration, nb_samples, format_name, stream counts, codec_long_name, codec_tag | gap (media-stream-fields) | as #93; ffprobe `-show_streams -show_format` names | struct per container; \n+| 95 | Renamed/transcoded audio: extension vs actual container/codec, MP3/Opus/Vorbis/AAC/AMR/FLAC/ALAC under a `.wav` name | partial (codec name only) | magic != extension (`ID3`/`ff fb` / `OggS` / `ftyp M4A` in `x.wav`) | magic routing; `file -k` (I) | high -- flavor \"transcoded, renamed\" |\n+| 96 | Multi-stream containers (MP4/MOV `trak`s, Matroska Tracks, Ogg multiplexed serials): per-stream codec/language/title/creation_time/handler; the odd stream | gap (media-multistream) | several `trak`/`TrackEntry`/BOS pages | box/EBML/page walk; ffprobe (M) | med-high -- \"the stream that breaks\n+| 97 | Audio inside mail: MIME `audio/*` attachment (base64) resolved as a member, `email -> attachment` refs | partial (email attachment metadata prebuilt; no media on decoded payload) | `Content-Type: audio/...`, `.eml -> voice.ogg` refs | `msg.walk()` + `get_payload(decode=True)` -> #93 | med-hi\n+| 98 | Recording equivalence across transcodes: same INFO/ID3/Vorbis title or correlation id, same duration/sample count, FLAC STREAMINFO MD5 / PCM data hash | gap (media-equivalence-synthesis) | synthesis text \"equivalent\", \"same recording\"; `Files: [...]` of audio members | lib.meta.synthesis + #\n \n ## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n \n@@ -137,7 +153,6 @@ d0 cf 11 e0 a1 b1 1a e1           CFB     olefile.OleFileIO(b).listdir() then ro\n   [Content_Types].xml               OOXML   rels / docProps core,app,custom / settings.xml.rels template\n   AppxManifest.xml                  MSIX    Identity Name/Publisher/Version\n   META-INF/MANIFEST.MF / classes.dex  JAR/APK (mobile lane)\n-  mimetype=application/epub+zip     EPUB    META-INF/container.xml -> OPF dc:*\n 4c 00 00 00 01 14 02 00           LNK     lib.meta.lnk / LnkParse3; LinkInfo vs IDList may disagree\n [InternetShortcut]                .url    URL= line\n 45 6c 66 46 69 6c 65 00 (ElfFile) EVTX    Evtx FileHeader(b,0).chunks() -> records -> rec.xml()\n@@ -155,14 +170,15 @@ ff d8 ff                          JPEG    SOF dims; APP1 Exif -> PIL getexif()/g\n 89 50 4e 47 0d 0a 1a 0a           PNG     IHDR@16; chunk walk tEXt/iTXt/zTXt/tIME; bytes after IEND\n 47 49 46 38 37/39 61              GIF     w,h u16LE @6/@8; 21 fe comment\n 42 4d (BM) / 00 00 01 00          BMP/ICO DIB w,h @18/@22 (i32) / count u16 @4\n-.. .. .. .. 66 74 79 70 (ftyp@4)  MP4/MOV box walk -> moov/mvhd creation_time (secs since 1904-01-01)\n-49 44 33 (ID3) / \"TAG\"@-128       MP3     ID3v2 frames TIT2/TPE1/COMM\n-52 49 46 46 .. 57 41 56 45        WAV     fmt (rate@24, ch@22), LIST/INFO\n-66 4c 61 43 (fLaC)                FLAC    STREAMINFO, block 4 VORBIS_COMMENT\n+media.* (GM fmt `media`, id family `audio`; ffprobe vocabulary, stream a:0 = first audio stream; route by MAGIC):\n+  52 49 46 46 .. 57 41 56 45 WAV  chunk walk @12 -> `fmt `: tag u16, ch u16, rate u32, bits u16 @+22; 0xFFFE -> SubFormat\n+     tag 1 -> pcm_u8/pcm_s16le/pcm_s24le/pcm_s32le (RIFX ..be), 3 pcm_f32le, 6 pcm_alaw, 7 pcm_mulaw, 0x55 mp3 (D17 pcm_s16le)\n+  49 44 33 / ff fb|f3|e3 = mp3; ff f1|f9 ADTS aac; 4f 67 67 53 OggS -> OpusHead/\\x01vorbis/\\x7fFLAC; 66 4c 61 43 flac;\n+  .. 66 74 79 70 (ftyp) -> stsd mp4a=aac / alac / Opus; mvhd time = s since 1904; 1a 45 df a3 MKV CodecID A_OPUS->opus\n+  #!AMR amr_nb / #!AMR-WB amr_wb; FORM..AIFF pcm_s16be (AIFC sowt = le); .snd au. ffprobe/sox (M); mutagen (I) for tags\n 1f 8b 08                          GZIP    FNAME if flg&8, MTIME u32LE@4, OS@9, ISIZE = last 4\n \"ustar\" @257                      TAR     tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b))\n-37 7a bc af 27 1c                 7z      major/minor @6/@7; 7z l -slt\n-52 61 72 21 1a 07 00 / 01 00      RAR4/5\n+37 7a bc af 27 1c / 52 61 72 21 1a 07 00|01 00   7z (ver @6/@7; 7z l -slt) / RAR4|RAR5\n \"CD001\" @0x8001                   ISO     PVD @0x8000: system id @+8, volume id @+40, creation date @+813\n \"conectix\" last 512 / vhdxfile / KDMV / QFI\\xfb  VHD/VHDX/VMDK/QCOW2   qemu-img info --output=json\n 53 51 4c 69 74 65 20 66 6f 72 6d 61 74 20 33 00  SQLite page size u16BE@16; sqlite3 .deserialize(b)\n@@ -180,27 +196,36 @@ Hex fields: `0x` + lowercase, zero-padded to the STRUCT width (`_u16_hex` 4 digi\n \n ## Readiness gaps\n \n-Ranking: priority 1 = plausible D17-D19 question with no extractor, or a harness blocker that silently fails a\n+Ranking: priority 1 = plausible D18-D20 question with no extractor, or a harness blocker that silently fails a\n whole family of prebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.\n \n ```json\n [\n-  {\"id\": \"email-fmt-alias\", \"concept\": \"GM fmt `email` -> prebuilt `eml` fields\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/email.py re-registering EVERY ('eml', f) field of lib/meta/prebuilt/eml.py under fmt 'email' (also 'mail', 'mime') with the same extractor. \n-  {\"id\": \"email-threading\", \"concept\": \"In-Reply-To / References / thread root / reply-forward flags\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email (+eml alias), fields in_reply_to, references (compact JSON list, stored order, each id with <>), references_count, thread_root_message_id \n-  {\"id\": \"email-mime-attachments\", \"concept\": \"MIME tree, attachment names/sizes/hashes/types\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email, fields mime_part_count, content_type (top-level, no params), mime_boundary, attachment_count, attachment_names (MIME order), attachment_content_\n-  {\"id\": \"mbox-collection\", \"concept\": \"MBOX / mailbox export: count, ids, duplicates, threads\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt mbox (alias mailbox), fields message_count, message_ids (file order, with <>), unique_message_id_count, duplicate_message_ids (sorted), thread_count, \n-  {\"id\": \"email-thread-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-message threading over several .eml members\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D16 flavor: 'rebuild which mail actually belongs together'. Add to lib.meta.synthesis: thread_groups(question, get_bytes) over the `Files: [...]` list -\n+  {\"id\": \"media-fmt-alias\", \"concept\": \"GM fmt `media` -> prebuilt `wav`/`mp3` fields + D17 codec name in lib\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/media.py registering fmt 'media' (aliases 'audio', 'av') that routes by MAGIC to the existing wav/mp3/gif... e\n+  {\"id\": \"media-stream-fields\", \"concept\": \"ffprobe-style stream/format fields for the first audio stream\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields primary_audio_sample_rate_hz (also _sample_rate), primary_audio_channels, primary_audio_channel_layout (ffprobe: mono/stereo/\n+  {\"id\": \"media-wav-deep\", \"concept\": \"WAV chunk-level metadata (BWF bext, fact, LIST/INFO, cue, iXML, data-vs-RIFF size, trailing bytes)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media + wav alias, fields riff_chunk_ids (file order JSON), info_title (INAM; D17 carried 'Huntress audio e\n+  {\"id\": \"media-renamed-containers\", \"concept\": \"Renamed/transcoded audio: actual container + codec vs the extension\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields container_format (by magic: wav/rf64/aiff/mp3/ogg/flac/mp4/matroska/amr/au/adts/caf/wma-asf), declared_extension, \n+  {\"id\": \"media-multistream\", \"concept\": \"Per-stream fields in multi-stream containers; the odd stream\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields stream_codec_names (JSON, container stream index order like ffprobe), audio_stream_codec_names, stream_languages (MP4 mdhd packe\n+  {\"id\": \"media-format-tags\", \"concept\": \"Container/stream tags: title, artist, comment, encoder, creation_time, language\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields tag_title, tag_artist, tag_album, tag_comment, tag_encoder, tag_date, tag_creation_time_utc, tag_<key> generi\n+  {\"id\": \"email-media-attachments\", \"concept\": \"Audio embedded in mail: MIME audio attachments + member resolution through .eml\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email (+eml/mime aliases), fields attachment_audio_codec_names (MIME order, via the media codec extractor on decoded \n+  {\"id\": \"media-equivalence-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-recording equivalence / odd-one-out synthesis\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Add to lib.meta.synthesis: equivalence_groups(question, get_bytes) over the `Files: [...]` audio members -> group by (1) shared title/correlation\n+  {\"id\": \"tool-ffprobe\", \"concept\": \"ffprobe/ffmpeg + sox for media ground truth\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"GM media fields use ffprobe vocabulary (`codec_name`, `sample_fmt`, `channel_layout`, `format_name`); ffprobe is NOT installed (mediainfo prints 'PCM'). Install a static ff\n+  {\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) exists (sha256 order asked D15, D16, D17; D17 Files = note + panel-001.png + managed-001.dll + \n   {\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Ta\n-  {\"id\": \"pe-debug-r