{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8BPFN6gxSDKT7BaPdwW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RyXZMPeDf2XUqoWfd7UeZh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\nt=open(p).read()\nFF='tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2'\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)==1,a[:70]; t=t.replace(a,b)\nrep('(as of D17, 2026-10-17)','(as of D17 post-run, 2026-10-18)')\n# likelihood paragraph\nrep(\"\"\"after that. Email fields remain warm (D16 family carries over in every timed kit).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"after that. Email fields remain warm (D16 family carries over in every timed kit).\n**D17 post-run:** single/TT/Mastery all asked only `pcm_s16le` (no transcode actually delivered) + the kit + synthesis.\nThe D17-night prebuild covered the whole audio flavor (fmt `media`/`audio`/`av`: codec/stream/format/tags/odd-stream,\n`email.attachment_audio_*`, `synthesis.*equivalence*`). Lesson of D16+D17: each new family lands under an ABSTRACT fmt\nword (`email`, `media`) with tool vocabulary (ffprobe). Next plausible (D18-D20): deeper `media.*` on a NON-WAV container\n(MP4/M4A voice memo atoms, AAC/MP3 codec params, WMA/ASF, AIFF/CAF), video/cover-art streams, images re-visited under an\nabstract `image.*` namespace (WebP/HEIC/TIFF, XMP DocumentID linking \"equivalent\" files), provenance (Zone.Identifier /\nquarantine xattr), and a synthesis key other than sha256 (size/time/duration order, codec grouping).\"\"\")\n# atlas rows\nrep(\"| seen D17 (`pcm_s16le`; day17 solver `_audio_codec`, not yet in lib) |\",\"| seen D17 (`pcm_s16le`; prebuilt media.py under fmt `media`/`audio`/`av`) |\")\nrep(\"day17 `solve.py:_audio_codec`; `ffprobe -show_entries stream=codec_name` (M)\", f\"`lib.meta` (`media`, `primary_audio_codec_name`); `{FF} -hide_banner -i f` (I, ffprobe names; no ffprobe)\")\nrep(\"| gap (media-stream-fields) |\",\"| prebuilt media_streams |\")\nrep(\"| partial (codec name only) | magic != extension\",\"| prebuilt media_ident | magic != extension\")\nrep(\"| gap (media-multistream) |\",\"| prebuilt media_streams (odd_stream_*) |\")\nrep(\"| partial (email attachment metadata prebuilt; no media on decoded payload) |\",\"| prebuilt email_media (`attachment_audio_*`) |\")\nrep(\"| gap (media-equivalence-synthesis) |\",\"| prebuilt synthesis_media (`equivalence_groups`, `odd_one_out*`) |\")\nrow_anchor=[l for l in t.split('\\n') if l.startswith('| 98 |')][0]\nrep(row_anchor, row_anchor+\"\"\"\n| 99 | MP4/M4A/MOV atoms: ftyp major/compatible brands, mvhd/mdhd creation time (1904 epoch), timescale, `©too`/`©xyz`, mdta keys (iPhone Voice Memos) | gap (mp4-mov-atoms) | `ftyp` @4, `moov`/`udta`/`meta`/`keys`/`ilst` | box walk struct; `ffmpeg -i` (I) shows tags | high -- \"voice notes\" are m4a |\n| 100 | Codec-level params: AAC ASC object type -> profile `LC`/`HE-AAC`, MP3 frame header + Xing/Info/LAME tag, bitrate mode | gap (media-codec-params) | `esds` DecoderSpecificInfo; `Xing`/`Info`/`LAME` @ first frame | bit parsing; `ffmpeg -i` (I) | med-high |\n| 101 | Other audio containers: ASF/WMA (wmav2), AIFF/AIFC COMM (80-bit rate, `sowt`/`NONE`), CAF `desc`, 3GP/AMR | gap (asf-aiff-caf-containers) | `30 26 b2 75 8e 66 cf 11` / `FORM..AIF[FC]` / `caff` | struct; `ffmpeg -i` (I) | med-high -- \"actual codecs\" |\n| 102 | Cover art / subtitles / chapters: attached_pic counted as a VIDEO stream (`mjpeg`/`png`), APIC, mov_text/subrip/ass streams, chapter titles | gap (subtitle-chapter-streams) | ID3 `APIC`, MP4 `covr`, MKV `Attachments`/`Chapters` | struct; ffprobe counts cover art in nb_streams | med |\n| 103 | XMP packets in any container: xmpMM DocumentID/InstanceID/OriginalDocumentID, History, CreatorTool, dc:creator/title | gap (xmp-packets) | `<x:xmpmeta` / `http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/` APP1 / PNG `iTXt XML:com.adobe.xmp` / MP4 `uuid` | regex the packet + `xml.etree`; `exiftool -xmp:all -j` (I) | med-high -- \"connect equivalent\" |\n| 104 | Modern images under an abstract `image.*` fmt: WebP VP8/VP8L/VP8X dims+chunks, TIFF IFD0, HEIC/AVIF `ispe`, ICC desc | gap (image-modern-containers) | `RIFF..WEBP`, `II*\\\\0`/`MM\\\\0*`, `ftyp heic/avif` | struct; `identify`/`exiftool` (I) | med |\n| 105 | Provenance: Zone.Identifier ADS (ZoneId/ReferrerUrl/HostUrl), macOS `com.apple.quarantine`, AppleDouble `._x` | gap (zone-identifier-motw) | `[ZoneTransfer]`; `00 05 16 07` | configparser / struct | med |\n| 106 | Disk images: VHD footer, VHDX, VMDK descriptor, QCOW2, ISO PVD | gap (disk-image-headers; ISO in archives-tar-7z-iso) | `conectix` / `vhdxfile` / `KDMV` / `QFI\\\\xfb` / `CD001` | struct; `qemu-img info` | low-med |\"\"\")\n# recognition cues (no new lines)\nrep(\"#!AMR amr_nb / #!AMR-WB amr_wb; FORM..AIFF pcm_s16be (AIFC sowt = le); .snd au. ffprobe/sox (M); mutagen (I) for tags\",\n    \"#!AMR amr_nb|amr_wb; FORM..AIFF pcm_s16be (AIFC sowt=le); 30 26 b2 75 ASF wmav2. Truth: tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/.../ffmpeg -i f\")\n# gaps json\nm=re.search(r'(## Readiness gaps.*?```json\\n)(.*?)(```)',t,re.S)\ngaps=json.loads(m.group(2))\nfor g in gaps:\n    if g['id']=='tool-ffprobe':\n        g['priority']=2\n        g['detail']=(f\"PARTLY SOLVED: ffmpeg 7.0.2 ships at {FF} (imageio-ffmpeg; not on PATH, no ffprobe). \"\n          \"`ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` prints ffprobe vocabulary (`Stream #0:0: Audio: pcm_s16le ([1][0][0][0] / 0x0001), 16000 Hz, mono, s16`, format tags) -- verified on D17. \"\n          \"Still wanted: a bin/ shim `ffmpeg` on PATH and a real ffprobe (static build) for `-show_streams -show_format -of json`; apt sox (soxi). Worker/offline verification only, never in-window.\")\n    if g['id']=='synthesis-siblings':\n        g['detail']=(\"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D17 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set). \"\n          \"D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). \"\n          \"D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings.\")\n    if g['id'] in ('media-fmt-alias','media-stream-fields','media-wav-deep','media-renamed-containers','media-multistream','media-format-tags','email-media-attachments','media-equivalence-synthesis'):\n        g['priority']=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"mp4-mov-atoms\",\"concept\":\"MP4/M4A/MOV/3GP atom metadata (voice memos, phone video)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt media (aliases audio, av, video, mp4, mov, quicktime). Box walk (size u32 BE, type; size 1 -> u64; size 0 -> to EOF). Fields: ftyp_major_brand (4 chars, trailing spaces kept as stored? emit rstrip'ed and also _raw), ftyp_minor_version, ftyp_compatible_brands (JSON, stored order), mvhd_creation_time_utc / mvhd_modification_time_utc (v0 u32 / v1 u64 seconds since 1904-01-01 -> ISO-8601 `Z`; ffprobe tag creation_time prints `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.000000Z`, emit that spelling under tag_creation_time), mvhd_timescale, mvhd_duration_seconds (duration/timescale, ffprobe-style 6 decimals), track_count, track_handler_types (JSON soun/vide/text), mdhd_languages (packed ISO-639-2 `und`), udta/ilst tags `©too` encoder, `©nam` title, `©day`, `©xyz` location (ISO 6709 string verbatim), mdta keys (`com.apple.quicktime.make/model/software/creationdate/location.ISO6709`) as tag_<key>. Pure struct; register via lib.meta like media_streams.py. Fixtures: build tiny m4a/mov with hand-packed boxes in the test (no ffmpeg needed).\"},\n {\"id\":\"media-codec-params\",\"concept\":\"Codec-level parameters (AAC profile, MP3 frame/Xing/LAME, Opus/Vorbis details) in ffprobe vocabulary\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt media (+audio/av). Fields: primary_audio_profile (AAC AudioSpecificConfig object type from esds/ADTS: 2 -> `LC`, 5 -> `HE-AAC`, 29 -> `HE-AACv2`, 1 -> `Main`; ffprobe spelling), primary_audio_codec_long_name (ffprobe strings: `AAC (Advanced Audio Coding)`, `MP3 (MPEG audio layer 3)`, `PCM signed 16-bit little-endian`, `Opus (Opus Interactive Audio Codec)`, `Vorbis`, `FLAC (Free Lossless Audio Codec)`), mp3_mpeg_version, mp3_layer, mp3_bitrate_kbps (first frame), mp3_vbr_header (`Xing`/`Info`/`VBRI`/none), mp3_lame_encoder (9-char LAME tag e.g. `LAME3.100`), mp3_frame_count, primary_audio_sample_fmt for compressed codecs (aac/mp3 -> `fltp`, opus -> `fltp`, vorbis -> `fltp`, flac -> s16/s32 by bps). Verify spellings offline with the bundled ffmpeg -i.\"},\n {\"id\":\"asf-aiff-caf-containers\",\"concept\":\"Other audio containers: ASF/WMA, AIFF/AIFC, CAF, AU, 3GP AMR\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt media (+audio/av; also fmt asf/aiff/caf aliases). Route by magic: ASF header GUID `30 26 b2 75 8e 66 cf 11 a6 d9 00 aa 00 62 ce 6c` -> Stream Properties audio WAVEFORMATEX tag (0x160 wmav1, 0x161 wmav2, 0x162 wmapro, 0x163 wmalossless, 0x0A wmavoice) + Content Description title/author/copyright/description + File Properties creation date (FILETIME) and play duration; AIFF `FORM....AIFF`/`AIFC` COMM: channels, numSampleFrames, sampleSize, 80-bit IEEE extended sample rate, AIFC compressionType (`NONE` -> pcm_s16be, `sowt` -> pcm_s16le, `fl32` -> pcm_f32be, `ulaw`/`alaw` -> pcm_mulaw/pcm_alaw, `ima4` -> adpcm_ima_qt) + NAME/AUTH/ANNO chunks; CAF `caff` desc chunk (float64 rate, formatID `lpcm`/`aac `/`alac`/`opus`/`ulaw`) + info chunk tags; Sun AU `.snd` encoding 1/2/3/27. Expose through primary_audio_codec_name/sample_rate/channels/container_format like the existing media modules (format_name ffprobe: `asf`, `aiff`, `caf`, `au`).\"},\n {\"id\":\"synthesis-order-siblings\",\"concept\":\"Synthesis questions with a non-sha256 key (size/time/duration order, codec grouping)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis*.py (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>-order|groups|<x>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): size_order (ascending bytes, ties -> filename), md5_order/sha1_order/sha512_order (generic algo from id), mtime_order (zip DOS mtime of each member from the container CD; also embedded timestamps: EXIF DateTimeOriginal, PDF CreationDate, email Date, mvhd creation), duration_order (media duration_seconds), codec_groups (JSON object codec_name -> sorted names), extension_mismatch_files (names whose magic != extension, file order), largest_file/smallest_file, newest_file/oldest_file. Descending only if the text says descending/newest first. Compact JSON.\"},\n {\"id\":\"xmp-packets\",\"concept\":\"XMP packet fields in any container (DocumentID lineage)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt xmp (also registered under jpeg/png/pdf/media/ooxml/image as xmp_<field>). Find `<x:xmpmeta` ... `</x:xmpmeta>` (or `<?xpacket begin` ... `<?xpacket end`) anywhere in the bytes (JPEG APP1 `http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/\\\\0`, PNG iTXt `XML:com.adobe.xmp`, PDF Metadata stream if uncompressed, MP4 `uuid` BE7ACFCB-97A9-42E8-9C71-999491E3AFAC, WAV `_PMX` chunk). Parse with xml.etree (namespaces by URI, rdf:Description attributes AND child elements, rdf:Seq/Alt/Bag -> lists). Fields: document_id, instance_id, original_document_id (verbatim incl. `xmp.did:`/`uuid:` prefixes), derived_from_document_id, history_actions (JSON, stored order), history_software_agents, creator_tool, create_date, modify_date, metadata_date (verbatim), dc_creator (JSON list), dc_title (x-default), dc_format. Synthesis helper: files sharing document_id/original_document_id.\"},\n {\"id\":\"image-modern-containers\",\"concept\":\"WebP / TIFF / HEIC-AVIF / ICC under an abstract `image.*` fmt\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt image (alias also for existing jpeg/png/gif/bmp fields: image.dimensions_pixels routes by magic to SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB) + webp, tiff, heic. WebP `RIFF....WEBP`: VP8 (frame tag, 14-bit w/h after `9d 01 2a`), VP8L (`2f` + 14-bit w-1/h-1), VP8X (canvas 24-bit w-1/h-1, flags ICC/alpha/EXIF/XMP/anim), chunk_ids JSON, has_exif/has_xmp/has_icc, animation frame_count. TIFF `II*\\\\0`/`MM\\\\0*`: byte_order, ifd0 ImageWidth/ImageLength/Make/Model/Software/DateTime/Artist, ifd_count. HEIC/AVIF `ftyp heic|heix|mif1|avif`: major_brand, ispe width x height of the primary item (pitm), item count, Exif item presence. ICC (APP2 ICC_PROFILE / PNG iCCP zlib / WebP ICCP): profile_description (desc/mluc), color_space, device_class, version. Answer formats like D4/D5: `<w>x<h>`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"subtitle-chapter-streams\",\"concept\":\"Cover art, subtitle and chapter streams (ffprobe stream accounting)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt media (+av/video). ffprobe counts an embedded cover (ID3 APIC, MP4 `covr`, FLAC PICTURE block, MKV attachment with image mime) as a VIDEO stream with codec_name `mjpeg`/`png` and disposition attached_pic=1 -> fields attached_pic_present, attached_pic_codec_name, attached_pic_mime_type, attached_pic_dimensions_pixels, nb_streams_including_cover (document the difference vs audio_stream_count). Subtitles: MP4 `tx3g` -> `mov_text`, MKV S_TEXT/UTF8 -> `subrip`, S_TEXT/ASS -> `ass`, S_TEXT/WEBVTT -> `webvtt`; fields subtitle_stream_count, subtitle_codec_names (stream order), subtitle_languages. Chapters: MP4 `chpl`/QuickTime chapter track, MKV EditionEntry/ChapterAtom -> chapter_count, chapter_titles (JSON), chapter_start_times_seconds.\"},\n {\"id\":\"zone-identifier-motw\",\"concept\":\"Download provenance: Zone.Identifier ADS, macOS quarantine, AppleDouble\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt zone_identifier (aliases motw, ads): text `[ZoneTransfer]` INI (UTF-8/UTF-16 with BOM): zone_id (int), zone_name (0 Local,1 Intranet,2 Trusted,3 Internet,4 Restricted), referrer_url, host_url, last_writer_package_family_name, app_zone_id -- values verbatim. Member names like `x.exe:Zone.Identifier` or `x.exe_Zone.Identifier`. fmt quarantine: `com.apple.quarantine` value `flags;hex_unix_time;agent;uuid` -> quarantine_flags_hex, quarantine_time_utc, quarantine_agent, quarantine_event_uuid. fmt appledouble: `00 05 16 07` header, entry table (id 2 resource fork, 9 Finder info with `ATTR` xattr block) -> xattr_names (JSON), xattr_<name> (UTF-8 if printable else hex), finder_type_creator.\"},\n {\"id\":\"archives-tar-7z-iso\",\"concept\":\"TAR / 7z / RAR / ISO9660-UDF headers (archives gap only produced gzip)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt archives were not registered by the earlier `archives` run (tar/7z/rar/iso have 0 fields). Separate modules: tar (ustar_magic, member_names stored order, member_sizes, member_mtimes_utc, member_modes_octal, member_unames/gnames, typeflags) via tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b)); 7z (signature_version `0.4`, next_header_offset/size, start_header_crc32_hex, has_encrypted_header when the next header is kEncodedHeader with AES coder 06f10701); rar (version 4|5, RAR5 main archive flags, file names when headers unencrypted, is_header_encrypted); iso (pvd system_id, volume_id, volume_set_id, publisher_id, application_id (strip spaces), volume_creation_date_utc from 17-byte dec-datetime @813 with GMT offset, volume_space_size, logical_block_size, joliet_present (SVD escape %/@ %/C %/E), udf_present (BEA01/NSR02/NSR03), root_member_names). fmt `archive` alias for all.\"},\n {\"id\":\"disk-image-headers\",\"concept\":\"Virtual disk headers (VHD/VHDX/VMDK/QCOW2)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt vhd (footer `conectix` in the last 512 B, or first 512 for dynamic copies): creator_application (4 chars), creator_version_u32_hex, creator_host_os, original_size_bytes, current_size_bytes, disk_type (2 fixed,3 dynamic,4 differencing), timestamp_utc (seconds since 2000-01-01), unique_id_guid, checksum_u32_hex. vhdx `vhdxfile` creator UTF-16 string @8. vmdk: sparse header `KDMV` + embedded descriptor text -> create_type, cid, parent_cid, ddb_uuid, ddb_virtual_hw_version, adapter_type, extent_files. qcow2 `QFI\\\\xfb`: version, size_bytes, backing_file_name, cluster_bits, crypt_method. fmt `disk` alias.\"},\n {\"id\":\"bplist-macos\",\"concept\":\"Apple property lists (binary/XML) and macOS artifacts\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt plist (aliases bplist, macos): parse `bplist00` (trailer last 32 B: offset size, ref size, num objects, top object, offset table; types int/real/date(2001 epoch)/data/ascii/utf16/uid/array/dict) and XML plists (plistlib.loads is stdlib -- allowed? if not, hand-parse). Fields: top_level_keys (JSON, stored order), value_<key> (path with `/` for nesting), cf_bundle_identifier, cf_bundle_executable, cf_bundle_short_version_string, ls_minimum_system_version, object_count. Covers Info.plist next to Mach-O (D-lane macho prebuilt) and .webloc (`URL`).\"},\n {\"id\":\"ics-vcard-v2\",\"concept\":\"iCalendar / vCard fields (re-attempt; previous run failed on `import zoneinfo`)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Same scope as the given-up `ics-vcard` gap but with NO zoneinfo/dateutil import: fmt ics (ical, calendar): uid, organizer (verbatim incl. `mailto:`), attendees (JSON stored order), dtstart, dtend (verbatim value, plus _utc only when the value ends in Z), summary, location, method, prodid, event_count; fmt vcard (vcf): fn, n, email (first), emails, tel, org, uid, version. RFC 5545 unfolding (CRLF + space/tab), `KEY;PARAM=..:value` split on the first unquoted colon, unescape `\\\\\\\\,` `\\\\\\;` `\\\\\\\\n`.\"},\n]\nids={g['id'] for g in gaps}\nfor g in new: assert g['id'] not in ids, g['id']\n# order: new p1 first, then existing p1, then rest by priority (stable)\nallg=new+gaps\nallg.sort(key=lambda g:g['priority'])\nbody='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in allg)+'\\n]\\n'\njson.loads(body)\nt=t[:m.start(2)]+body+t[m.end(2):]\nrep(\"Ranking: priority 1 = plausible D18-D20 question with no extractor,\",\"Ranking (D17 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D18-D20 question with no extractor,\")\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\nF=reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md; awk '/^## Recognition cues/{a=NR} /^## Readiness gaps/{print \"cues lines\",NR-a-1}' $F; wc -l $F"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2329,"cache_read_input_tokens":89663,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2329},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef86878e-e33c-4f7a-a4f5-f24bdd265e55","uuid":"48e26c7d-9384-4fb4-8c62-9e88f2513373","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:11:32.138Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8BPEvZ2b8RWWAwpEag2","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RyXZMPeDf2XUqoWfd7UeZh":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\nt=open(p).read()\nFF='tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2'\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)==1,a[:70]; t=t.replace(a,b)\nrep('(as of D17, 2026-10-17)','(as of D17 post-run, 2026-10-18)')\n# likelihood paragraph\nrep(\"\"\"after that. Email fields remain warm (D16 family carries over in every timed kit).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"after that. Email fields remain warm (D16 family carries over in every timed kit).\n**D17 post-run:** single/TT/Mastery all asked only `pcm_s16le` (no transcode actually delivered) + the kit + synthesis.\nThe D17-night prebuild covered the whole audio flavor (fmt `media`/`audio`/`av`: codec/stream/format/tags/odd-stream,\n`email.attachment_audio_*`, `synthesis.*equivalence*`). Lesson of D16+D17: each new family lands under an ABSTRACT fmt\nword (`email`, `media`) with tool vocabulary (ffprobe). Next plausible (D18-D20): deeper `media.*` on a NON-WAV container\n(MP4/M4A voice memo atoms, AAC/MP3 codec params, WMA/ASF, AIFF/CAF), video/cover-art streams, images re-visited under an\nabstract `image.*` namespace (WebP/HEIC/TIFF, XMP DocumentID linking \"equivalent\" files), provenance (Zone.Identifier /\nquarantine xattr), and a synthesis key other than sha256 (size/time/duration order, codec grouping).\"\"\")\n# atlas rows\nrep(\"| seen D17 (`pcm_s16le`; day17 solver `_audio_codec`, not yet in lib) |\",\"| seen D17 (`pcm_s16le`; prebuilt media.py under fmt `media`/`audio`/`av`) |\")\nrep(\"day17 `solve.py:_audio_codec`; `ffprobe -show_entries stream=codec_name` (M)\", f\"`lib.meta` (`media`, `primary_audio_codec_name`); `{FF} -hide_banner -i f` (I, ffprobe names; no ffprobe)\")\nrep(\"| gap (media-stream-fields) |\",\"| prebuilt media_streams |\")\nrep(\"| partial (codec name only) | magic != extension\",\"| prebuilt media_ident | magic != extension\")\nrep(\"| gap (media-multistream) |\",\"| prebuilt media_streams (odd_stream_*) |\")\nrep(\"| partial (email attachment metadata prebuilt; no media on decoded payload) |\",\"| prebuilt email_media (`attachment_audio_*`) |\")\nrep(\"| gap (media-equivalence-synthesis) |\",\"| prebuilt synthesis_media (`equivalence_groups`, `odd_one_out*`) |\")\nrow_anchor=[l for l in t.split('\\n') if l.startswith('| 98 |')][0]\nrep(row_anchor, row_anchor+\"\"\"\n| 99 | MP4/M4A/MOV atoms: ftyp major/compatible brands, mvhd/mdhd creation time (1904 epoch), timescale, `©too`/`©xyz`, mdta keys (iPhone Voice Memos) | gap (mp4-mov-atoms) | `ftyp` @4, `moov`/`udta`/`meta`/`keys`/`ilst` | box walk struct; `ffmpeg -i` (I) shows tags | high -- \"voice notes\" are m4a |\n| 100 | Codec-level params: AAC ASC object type -> profile `LC`/`HE-AAC`, MP3 frame header + Xing/Info/LAME tag, bitrate mode | gap (media-codec-params) | `esds` DecoderSpecificInfo; `Xing`/`Info`/`LAME` @ first frame | bit parsing; `ffmpeg -i` (I) | med-high |\n| 101 | Other audio containers: ASF/WMA (wmav2), AIFF/AIFC COMM (80-bit rate, `sowt`/`NONE`), CAF `desc`, 3GP/AMR | gap (asf-aiff-caf-containers) | `30 26 b2 75 8e 66 cf 11` / `FORM..AIF[FC]` / `caff` | struct; `ffmpeg -i` (I) | med-high -- \"actual codecs\" |\n| 102 | Cover art / subtitles / chapters: attached_pic counted as a VIDEO stream (`mjpeg`/`png`), APIC, mov_text/subrip/ass streams, chapter titles | gap (subtitle-chapter-streams) | ID3 `APIC`, MP4 `covr`, MKV `Attachments`/`Chapters` | struct; ffprobe counts cover art in nb_streams | med |\n| 103 | XMP packets in any container: xmpMM DocumentID/InstanceID/OriginalDocumentID, History, CreatorTool, dc:creator/title | gap (xmp-packets) | `<x:xmpmeta` / `http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/` APP1 / PNG `iTXt XML:com.adobe.xmp` / MP4 `uuid` | regex the packet + `xml.etree`; `exiftool -xmp:all -j` (I) | med-high -- \"connect equivalent\" |\n| 104 | Modern images under an abstract `image.*` fmt: WebP VP8/VP8L/VP8X dims+chunks, TIFF IFD0, HEIC/AVIF `ispe`, ICC desc | gap (image-modern-containers) | `RIFF..WEBP`, `II*\\\\0`/`MM\\\\0*`, `ftyp heic/avif` | struct; `identify`/`exiftool` (I) | med |\n| 105 | Provenance: Zone.Identifier ADS (ZoneId/ReferrerUrl/HostUrl), macOS `com.apple.quarantine`, AppleDouble `._x` | gap (zone-identifier-motw) | `[ZoneTransfer]`; `00 05 16 07` | configparser / struct | med |\n| 106 | Disk images: VHD footer, VHDX, VMDK descriptor, QCOW2, ISO PVD | gap (disk-image-headers; ISO in archives-tar-7z-iso) | `conectix` / `vhdxfile` / `KDMV` / `QFI\\\\xfb` / `CD001` | struct; `qemu-img info` | low-med |\"\"\")\n# recognition cues (no new lines)\nrep(\"#!AMR amr_nb / #!AMR-WB amr_wb; FORM..AIFF pcm_s16be (AIFC sowt = le); .snd au. ffprobe/sox (M); mutagen (I) for tags\",\n    \"#!AMR amr_nb|amr_wb; FORM..AIFF pcm_s16be (AIFC sowt=le); 30 26 b2 75 ASF wmav2. Truth: tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/.../ffmpeg -i f\")\n# gaps json\nm=re.search(r'(## Readiness gaps.*?```json\\n)(.*?)(```)',t,re.S)\ngaps=json.loads(m.group(2))\nfor g in gaps:\n    if g['id']=='tool-ffprobe':\n        g['priority']=2\n        g['detail']=(f\"PARTLY SOLVED: ffmpeg 7.0.2 ships at {FF} (imageio-ffmpeg; not on PATH, no ffprobe). \"\n          \"`ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` prints ffprobe vocabulary (`Stream #0:0: Audio: pcm_s16le ([1][0][0][0] / 0x0001), 16000 Hz, mono, s16`, format tags) -- verified on D17. \"\n          \"Still wanted: a bin/ shim `ffmpeg` on PATH and a real ffprobe (static build) for `-show_streams -show_format -of json`; apt sox (soxi). Worker/offline verification only, never in-window.\")\n    if g['id']=='synthesis-siblings':\n        g['detail']=(\"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D17 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set). \"\n          \"D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). \"\n          \"D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings.\")\n    if g['id'] in ('media-fmt-alias','media-stream-fields','media-wav-deep','media-renamed-containers','media-multistream','media-format-tags','email-media-attachments','media-equivalence-synthesis'):\n        g['priority']=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"mp4-mov-atoms\",\"concept\":\"MP4/M4A/MOV/3GP atom metadata (voice memos, phone video)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt media (aliases audio, av, video, mp4, mov, quicktime). Box walk (size u32 BE, type; size 1 -> u64; size 0 -> to EOF). Fields: ftyp_major_brand (4 chars, trailing spaces kept as stored? emit rstrip'ed and also _raw), ftyp_minor_version, ftyp_compatible_brands (JSON, stored order), mvhd_creation_time_utc / mvhd_modification_time_utc (v0 u32 / v1 u64 seconds since 1904-01-01 -> ISO-8601 `Z`; ffprobe tag creation_time prints `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.000000Z`, emit that spelling under tag_creation_time), mvhd_timescale, mvhd_duration_seconds (duration/timescale, ffprobe-style 6 decimals), track_count, track_handler_types (JSON soun/vide/text), mdhd_languages (packed ISO-639-2 `und`), udta/ilst tags `©too` encoder, `©nam` title, `©day`, `©xyz` location (ISO 6709 string verbatim), mdta keys (`com.apple.quicktime.make/model/software/creationdate/location.ISO6709`) as tag_<key>. Pure struct; register via lib.meta like media_streams.py. Fixtures: build tiny m4a/mov with hand-packed boxes in the test (no ffmpeg needed).\"},\n {\"id\":\"media-codec-params\",\"concept\":\"Codec-level parameters (AAC profile, MP3 frame/Xing/LAME, Opus/Vorbis details) in ffprobe vocabulary\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt media (+audio/av). Fields: primary_audio_profile (AAC AudioSpecificConfig object type from esds/ADTS: 2 -> `LC`, 5 -> `HE-AAC`, 29 -> `HE-AACv2`, 1 -> `Main`; ffprobe spelling), primary_audio_codec_long_name (ffprobe strings: `AAC (Advanced Audio Coding)`, `MP3 (MPEG audio layer 3)`, `PCM signed 16-bit little-endian`, `Opus (Opus Interactive Audio Codec)`, `Vorbis`, `FLAC (Free Lossless Audio Codec)`), mp3_mpeg_version, mp3_layer, mp3_bitrate_kbps (first frame), mp3_vbr_header (`Xing`/`Info`/`VBRI`/none), mp3_lame_encoder (9-char LAME tag e.g. `LAME3.100`), mp3_frame_count, primary_audio_sample_fmt for compressed codecs (aac/mp3 -> `fltp`, opus -> `fltp`, vorbis -> `fltp`, flac -> s16/s32 by bps). Verify spellings offline with the bundled ffmpeg -i.\"},\n {\"id\":\"asf-aiff-caf-containers\",\"concept\":\"Other audio containers: ASF/WMA, AIFF/AIFC, CAF, AU, 3GP AMR\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt media (+audio/av; also fmt asf/aiff/caf aliases). Route by magic: ASF header GUID `30 26 b2 75 8e 66 cf 11 a6 d9 00 aa 00 62 ce 6c` -> Stream Properties audio WAVEFORMATEX tag (0x160 wmav1, 0x161 wmav2, 0x162 wmapro, 0x163 wmalossless, 0x0A wmavoice) + Content Description title/author/copyright/description + File Properties creation date (FILETIME) and play duration; AIFF `FORM....AIFF`/`AIFC` COMM: channels, numSampleFrames, sampleSize, 80-bit IEEE extended sample rate, AIFC compressionType (`NONE` -> pcm_s16be, `sowt` -> pcm_s16le, `fl32` -> pcm_f32be, `ulaw`/`alaw` -> pcm_mulaw/pcm_alaw, `ima4` -> adpcm_ima_qt) + NAME/AUTH/ANNO chunks; CAF `caff` desc chunk (float64 rate, formatID `lpcm`/`aac `/`alac`/`opus`/`ulaw`) + info chunk tags; Sun AU `.snd` encoding 1/2/3/27. Expose through primary_audio_codec_name/sample_rate/channels/container_format like the existing media modules (format_name ffprobe: `asf`, `aiff`, `caf`, `au`).\"},\n {\"id\":\"synthesis-order-siblings\",\"concept\":\"Synthesis questions with a non-sha256 key (size/time/duration order, codec grouping)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis*.py (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>-order|groups|<x>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): size_order (ascending bytes, ties -> filename), md5_order/sha1_order/sha512_order (generic algo from id), mtime_order (zip DOS mtime of each member from the container CD; also embedded timestamps: EXIF DateTimeOriginal, PDF CreationDate, email Date, mvhd creation), duration_order (media duration_seconds), codec_groups (JSON object codec_name -> sorted names), extension_mismatch_files (names whose magic != extension, file order), largest_file/smallest_file, newest_file/oldest_file. Descending only if the text says descending/newest first. Compact JSON.\"},\n {\"id\":\"xmp-packets\",\"concept\":\"XMP packet fields in any container (DocumentID lineage)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt xmp (also registered under jpeg/png/pdf/media/ooxml/image as xmp_<field>). Find `<x:xmpmeta` ... `</x:xmpmeta>` (or `<?xpacket begin` ... `<?xpacket end`) anywhere in the bytes (JPEG APP1 `http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/\\\\0`, PNG iTXt `XML:com.adobe.xmp`, PDF Metadata stream if uncompressed, MP4 `uuid` BE7ACFCB-97A9-42E8-9C71-999491E3AFAC, WAV `_PMX` chunk). Parse with xml.etree (namespaces by URI, rdf:Description attributes AND child elements, rdf:Seq/Alt/Bag -> lists). Fields: document_id, instance_id, original_document_id (verbatim incl. `xmp.did:`/`uuid:` prefixes), derived_from_document_id, history_actions (JSON, stored order), history_software_agents, creator_tool, create_date, modify_date, metadata_date (verbatim), dc_creator (JSON list), dc_title (x-default), dc_format. Synthesis helper: files sharing document_id/original_document_id.\"},\n {\"id\":\"image-modern-containers\",\"concept\":\"WebP / TIFF / HEIC-AVIF / ICC under an abstract `image.*` fmt\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt image (alias also for existing jpeg/png/gif/bmp fields: image.dimensions_pixels routes by magic to SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB) + webp, tiff, heic. WebP `RIFF....WEBP`: VP8 (frame tag, 14-bit w/h after `9d 01 2a`), VP8L (`2f` + 14-bit w-1/h-1), VP8X (canvas 24-bit w-1/h-1, flags ICC/alpha/EXIF/XMP/anim), chunk_ids JSON, has_exif/has_xmp/has_icc, animation frame_count. TIFF `II*\\\\0`/`MM\\\\0*`: byte_order, ifd0 ImageWidth/ImageLength/Make/Model/Software/DateTime/Artist, ifd_count. HEIC/AVIF `ftyp heic|heix|mif1|avif`: major_brand, ispe width x height of the primary item (pitm), item count, Exif item presence. ICC (APP2 ICC_PROFILE / PNG iCCP zlib / WebP ICCP): profile_description (desc/mluc), color_space, device_class, version. Answer formats like D4/D5: `<w>x<h>`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"subtitle-chapter-streams\",\"concept\":\"Cover art, subtitle and chapter streams (ffprobe stream accounting)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt media (+av/video). ffprobe counts an embedded cover (ID3 APIC, MP4 `covr`, FLAC PICTURE block, MKV attachment with image mime) as a VIDEO stream with codec_name `mjpeg`/`png` and disposition attached_pic=1 -> fields attached_pic_present, attached_pic_codec_name, attached_pic_mime_type, attached_pic_dimensions_pixels, nb_streams_including_cover (document the difference vs audio_stream_count). Subtitles: MP4 `tx3g` -> `mov_text`, MKV S_TEXT/UTF8 -> `subrip`, S_TEXT/ASS -> `ass`, S_TEXT/WEBVTT -> `webvtt`; fields subtitle_stream_count, subtitle_codec_names (stream order), subtitle_languages. Chapters: MP4 `chpl`/QuickTime chapter track, MKV EditionEntry/ChapterAtom -> chapter_count, chapter_titles (JSON), chapter_start_times_seconds.\"},\n {\"id\":\"zone-identifier-motw\",\"concept\":\"Download provenance: Zone.Identifier ADS, macOS quarantine, AppleDouble\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt zone_identifier (aliases motw, ads): text `[ZoneTransfer]` INI (UTF-8/UTF-16 with BOM): zone_id (int), zone_name (0 Local,1 Intranet,2 Trusted,3 Internet,4 Restricted), referrer_url, host_url, last_writer_package_family_name, app_zone_id -- values verbatim. Member names like `x.exe:Zone.Identifier` or `x.exe_Zone.Identifier`. fmt quarantine: `com.apple.quarantine` value `flags;hex_unix_time;agent;uuid` -> quarantine_flags_hex, quarantine_time_utc, quarantine_agent, quarantine_event_uuid. fmt appledouble: `00 05 16 07` header, entry table (id 2 resource fork, 9 Finder info with `ATTR` xattr block) -> xattr_names (JSON), xattr_<name> (UTF-8 if printable else hex), finder_type_creator.\"},\n {\"id\":\"archives-tar-7z-iso\",\"concept\":\"TAR / 7z / RAR / ISO9660-UDF headers (archives gap only produced gzip)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt archives were not registered by the earlier `archives` run (tar/7z/rar/iso have 0 fields). Separate modules: tar (ustar_magic, member_names stored order, member_sizes, member_mtimes_utc, member_modes_octal, member_unames/gnames, typeflags) via tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b)); 7z (signature_version `0.4`, next_header_offset/size, start_header_crc32_hex, has_encrypted_header when the next header is kEncodedHeader with AES coder 06f10701); rar (version 4|5, RAR5 main archive flags, file names when headers unencrypted, is_header_encrypted); iso (pvd system_id, volume_id, volume_set_id, publisher_id, application_id (strip spaces), volume_creation_date_utc from 17-byte dec-datetime @813 with GMT offset, volume_space_size, logical_block_size, joliet_present (SVD escape %/@ %/C %/E), udf_present (BEA01/NSR02/NSR03), root_member_names). fmt `archive` alias for all.\"},\n {\"id\":\"disk-image-headers\",\"concept\":\"Virtual disk headers (VHD/VHDX/VMDK/QCOW2)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt vhd (footer `conectix` in the last 512 B, or first 512 for dynamic copies): creator_application (4 chars), creator_version_u32_hex, creator_host_os, original_size_bytes, current_size_bytes, disk_type (2 fixed,3 dynamic,4 differencing), timestamp_utc (seconds since 2000-01-01), unique_id_guid, checksum_u32_hex. vhdx `vhdxfile` creator UTF-16 string @8. vmdk: sparse header `KDMV` + embedded descriptor text -> create_type, cid, parent_cid, ddb_uuid, ddb_virtual_hw_version, adapter_type, extent_files. qcow2 `QFI\\\\xfb`: version, size_bytes, backing_file_name, cluster_bits, crypt_method. fmt `disk` alias.\"},\n {\"id\":\"bplist-macos\",\"concept\":\"Apple property lists (binary/XML) and macOS artifacts\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt plist (aliases bplist, macos): parse `bplist00` (trailer last 32 B: offset size, ref size, num objects, top object, offset table; types int/real/date(2001 epoch)/data/ascii/utf16/uid/array/dict) and XML plists (plistlib.loads is stdlib -- allowed? if not, hand-parse). Fields: top_level_keys (JSON, stored order), value_<key> (path with `/` for nesting), cf_bundle_identifier, cf_bundle_executable, cf_bundle_short_version_string, ls_minimum_system_version, object_count. Covers Info.plist next to Mach-O (D-lane macho prebuilt) and .webloc (`URL`).\"},\n {\"id\":\"ics-vcard-v2\",\"concept\":\"iCalendar / vCard fields (re-attempt; previous run failed on `import zoneinfo`)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Same scope as the given-up `ics-vcard` gap but with NO zoneinfo/dateutil import: fmt ics (ical, calendar): uid, organizer (verbatim incl. `mailto:`), attendees (JSON stored order), dtstart, dtend (verbatim value, plus _utc only when the value ends in Z), summary, location, method, prodid, event_count; fmt vcard (vcf): fn, n, email (first), emails, tel, org, uid, version. RFC 5545 unfolding (CRLF + space/tab), `KEY;PARAM=..:value` split on the first unquoted colon, unescape `\\\\\\\\,` `\\\\\\\\;` `\\\\\\\\n`.\"},\n]\nids={g['id'] for g in gaps}\nfor g in new: assert g['id'] not in ids, g['id']\n# order: new p1 first, then existing p1, then rest by priority (stable)\nallg=new+gaps\nallg.sort(key=lambda g:g['priority'])\nbody='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in allg)+'\\n]\\n'\njson.loads(body)\nt=t[:m.start(2)]+body+t[m.end(2):]\nrep(\"Ranking: priority 1 = plausible D18-D20 question with no extractor,\",\"Ranking (D17 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D18-D20 question with no extractor,\")\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\nF=reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md; awk '/^## Recognition cues/{a=NR} /^## Readiness gaps/{print \"cues lines\",NR-a-1}' $F; wc -l $F"}}}
