{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8BW4VgWsebmw8rdY8e4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both metadata-forensics files. Nothing else was touched, and no tests or GM calls were run.\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md`** (223 lines): the Day 17 \"Hear Me Out\" entry, the variant axes and the pitfalls were mostly already written before this run (the 2-day-repeat synthesis/per-set-root note was there). I added three things:\n   - There is an ffmpeg 7.0.2 binary at `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2`. Running it with `-hide_banner -i <file>` prints codec names the way ffprobe does: on the Day 17 file it shows `Stream #0:0: Audio: pcm_s16le`. There is still no ffprobe.\n   - The `lib.meta` media fields now exist under `media`/`audio`/`av`.\n   - A new pitfall: each new family has arrived under a general format word (`email`, `media`), so expect `image`, `video`, `archive` or `disk` next.\n\n   I also merged the Day 15 and Day 16 entries to keep the file short.\n2. **Coverage atlas, table and cues**: atlas rows 94–98 now show what the overnight build covered (stream/format fields, renamed containers, multi-stream, audio attached to mail, matching recordings). I added rows 99–106 for areas we haven't seen yet: MP4/M4A atoms, codec details, ASF/AIFF/CAF, cover art and subtitles, XMP, modern image formats, download-origin markers (Zone.Identifier) and disk images. I added a D18–D20 forecast paragraph and fixed the media cue lines; the recognition cues stay at 59 lines.\n3. **Coverage atlas, readiness gaps**: all 40 earlier prebuild gaps had already been built or given up, so the prebuild queue was empty. I added 12 new prebuild gaps, so 12 are now pending (target is at least 8). The four at priority 1 are:\n   - `mp4-mov-atoms` (metadata inside M4A/MP4 files, e.g. phone voice memos)\n   - `media-codec-params` (AAC profile, MP3 frame and LAME encoder details)\n   - `asf-aiff-caf-containers` (other audio containers)\n   - `synthesis-order-siblings` (cross-file questions that order by size, time or duration instead of sha256)\n\n   Priority 2 holds XMP, images, subtitles/cover art, Zone.Identifier and TAR/7z/RAR/ISO. Priority 3 holds disk images, Apple plists and `ics-vcard-v2`, which retries a gap that failed twice on a disallowed `zoneinfo` import. I moved the built Day 17 media gaps and `tool-ffprobe` down to priority 2. The JSON block parses with the same keys and no duplicate ids."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":102192,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":921},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef86878e-e33c-4f7a-a4f5-f24bdd265e55","uuid":"0934313f-4d6d-46eb-87de-e9fe32041593","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:11:56.025Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8BW4CpYxPayT9GvW1ww"}
